msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:23
msgid "Pricing and Plans"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:25
msgid ""
"The free plan includes 2,000 Zeta predictions per month. The [Pro plan](../"
"ai/plans-and-usage.md) removes this limit. See [Zed's pricing page](https://"
"zed.dev/pricing) for details."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:27
msgid "Switching Modes"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:29
msgid "Zed's Edit Prediction comes with two different display modes:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:31
msgid ""
"`eager` (default): predictions are displayed inline as long as it doesn't "
"conflict with language server completions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:32
msgid ""
"`subtle`: predictions only appear inline when holding a modifier key (`alt` "
"by default)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:34
msgid "Toggle between them via the `mode` key:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:37 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:273
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:313
msgid "\"edit_predictions\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:38
msgid "\"mode\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:38
msgid "\"eager\" // or \"subtle\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:42
msgid "Or directly via the UI through the status bar menu:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:44
msgid ""
"![Edit Prediction status bar menu, with the modes toggle.](https://zed.dev/"
"img/edit-prediction/status-bar-menu.webp)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:46
msgid "Note that edit prediction modes work with any prediction provider."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:48
msgid "Conflict With Other `tab` Actions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:50
msgid ""
"By default, when `tab` would normally perform a different action, Zed "
"requires a modifier key to accept predictions:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:52
msgid "When the language server completions menu is visible."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:53
msgid "When your cursor isn't at the right indentation level."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:55
msgid ""
"In these cases, `alt-tab` is used instead to accept the prediction. When the "
"language server completions menu is open, holding `alt` first will cause it "
"to temporarily disappear in order to preview the prediction within the "
"buffer."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:57
msgid ""
"On Linux, `alt-tab` is often used by the window manager for switching "
"windows, so `alt-l` is provided as the default binding for accepting "
"predictions. `tab` and `alt-tab` also work, but aren't displayed by default."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:59
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">editor: accept next word edit prediction</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-cmd-right|alt-k</kbd>) can be used to accept the "
"current edit prediction up to the next word boundary. <code "
"class=\"hljs\">editor: accept next line edit prediction</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-cmd-down|alt-j</kbd>) can be used to accept the "
"current edit prediction up to the new line boundary."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:62
msgid "Configuring Edit Prediction Keybindings"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:64
msgid ""
"By default, `tab` is used to accept edit predictions. You can use another "
"keybinding by inserting this in your keymap:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:68 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:81
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:95 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:108
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:122 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:139
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:146 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:152
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:163 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:169
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:183 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:191
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:224
msgid "\"context\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:68 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:139
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:183
msgid "\"Editor && edit_prediction\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:69 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:82
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:96 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:109
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:123 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:140
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:147 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:153
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:164 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:170
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:184 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:192
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:210 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:225
msgid "\"bindings\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:70
msgid ""
"// Here we also allow `alt-enter` to accept the prediction\n"
"    \"alt-enter\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:71 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:99
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:111 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:124
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:141 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:185
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:193 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:226
msgid "\"editor::AcceptEditPrediction\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:76
msgid ""
"When there's a [conflict with the `tab` key](#edit-predictions-conflict), "
"Zed uses a different key context to accept keybindings "
"(`edit_prediction_conflict`). If you want to use a different one, you can "
"insert this in your keymap:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:81 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:95
#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:191 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:224
msgid "\"Editor && edit_prediction_conflict\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:83
msgid "\"ctrl-enter\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:83
msgid "\"editor::AcceptEditPrediction\" // Example of a modified keybinding\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:88
msgid ""
"If your keybinding contains a modifier (`ctrl` in the example above), it "
"will also be used to preview the edit prediction and temporarily hide the "
"language server completion menu."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:90
msgid ""
"You can also bind this action to keybind without a modifier. In that case, "
"Zed will use the default modifier (`alt`) to preview the edit prediction."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:97
msgid ""
"// Here we bind tab to accept even when there's a language server "
"completion\n"
"    // or the cursor isn't at the correct indentation level\n"
"    \"tab\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:104
msgid ""
"To maintain the use of the modifier key for accepting predictions when there "
"is a language server completions menu, but allow `tab` to accept predictions "
"regardless of cursor position, you can specify the context further with "
"`showing_completions`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:108
msgid "\"Editor && edit_prediction_conflict && !showing_completions\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:110
msgid ""
"// Here we don't require a modifier unless there's a language server "
"completion\n"
"    \"tab\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:116
msgid "Keybinding Example: Always Use Tab"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:118
msgid ""
"If you want to use `tab` to always accept edit predictions, you can use the "
"following keybinding:"
