#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:171 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:185
msgid "\"tab\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:129
msgid ""
"This will make `tab` work to accept edit predictions _even when_ you're also "
"seeing language server completions. That means that you need to rely on "
"`enter` for accepting the latter."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:132
msgid "Keybinding Example: Always Use Alt-Tab"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:134
msgid ""
"The keybinding example below causes `alt-tab` to always be used instead of "
"sometimes using `tab`. You might want this in order to have just one "
"(alternative) keybinding to use for accepting edit predictions, since the "
"behavior of `tab` varies based on context."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:141 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:193
msgid "\"alt-tab\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:144
msgid "// Bind `tab` back to its original behavior.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:146
msgid "\"Editor\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:148
msgid "\"editor::Tab\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:152
msgid "\"Editor && showing_completions\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:154
msgid "\"editor::ComposeCompletion\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:159
msgid ""
"If you are using [Vim mode](../vim.md), then additional bindings are needed "
"after the above to return `tab` to its original behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:163
msgid "\"(VimControl && !menu) || vim_mode == replace || vim_mode == waiting\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:165
msgid "\"vim::Tab\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:169
msgid "\"vim_mode == literal\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:171
msgid "\"vim::Literal\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:171
msgid "\"\\u0009\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:176
msgid "Keybinding Example: Displaying Tab and Alt-Tab on Linux"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:178
msgid ""
"While `tab` and `alt-tab` are supported on Linux, `alt-l` is displayed "
"instead. If your window manager does not reserve `alt-tab`, and you would "
"prefer to use `tab` and `alt-tab`, include these bindings in `keymap.json`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:186 src/ai/edit-prediction.md:194
msgid ""
"// Optional: This makes the default `alt-l` binding do nothing.\n"
"      \"alt-l\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:200
msgid "Missing keybind"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:202
msgid ""
"Zed requires at least one keybinding for the <code class=\"hljs\">editor: "
"accept edit prediction</code> action in both the `Editor && edit_prediction` "
"and `Editor && edit_prediction_conflict` contexts ([learn more above](#edit-"
"predictions-keybinding))."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/edit-prediction.md:204
msgid ""
"If you have previously bound the default keybindings to different actions in "
"the global context, you will not be able to preview or accept edit "
